@*
    MarkdownContent — renders a safe markdown subset as HTML elements.

    Used by TokenRenderer when IsStreaming=false (canonical / final text only).
    During streaming the plain-text span path in TokenRenderer is unchanged —
    this component is never called on the hot streaming path.

    Safety contract:
      • All text content is passed through Blazor's RenderTreeBuilder.AddContent,
        which HTML-encodes every string. MarkupString is NOT used anywhere in
        this component or MarkdownTokenizer.
      • Output elements are a fixed safe subset: p, strong, em, ol, ul, li, br.
        No links, no script, no style attributes, no inline event handlers.
      • The CSP enforcement in production is unaffected because no inline markup
        is injected.

    The component emits a single <div class="markdown-content"> wrapper and
    lets the MarkdownTokenizer own the block structure (p / ol / ul). MudText
    is not used as a container here to avoid double-wrapping with an extra
    block element, which is both invalid HTML (p-in-p) and makes test
    assertions on block counts unreliable.

    ADR-0026 § 6 — delight surface lock (sub-component of WizardAnswerStream)
    ADR-0008     — MudBlazor strict for chrome; prose rendered via tokenizer
                    block elements styled via .markdown-content class
*@

@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Text))
{
    <div class="markdown-content" data-testid="markdown-content">
        @MarkdownTokenizer.Render(Text)
    </div>
}

@code {
    // The canonical answer text to render. Expected to be the Final.Answer.Text
    // (post-guardrail, post-citation-strip); never raw streaming delta text.
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Text { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
